<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Lindwyrm ~ Nagel Seed

''One of the seeds.'' This meme records a render seed and its returns — ''not'' a canonical
appearance. The Patroness's form stands ''unrecorded by design'': witnesses disagree, and she
corrects none of them ([[the-lindwyrm|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/npcs/the-lindwyrm]]).

''So read what follows as one witness's account, painted.'' A Nagel Lindwyrm joins the pile of
mutually incompatible descriptions rather than settling it. The pile ''is'' the canon.

''Why the register suits her.'' Nagel's method runs by ''subtraction'' — the nose bridge goes, the
ear cartilage goes, the shading goes, the background goes, until only the minimum remains, and the
face reads ''more'' present for it. A Nagel portrait declines to be fully specified and gains
authority by declining. That stands as the Lindwyrm's own law, executed as technique.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/prompt>>

!! The Prompt (verbatim)

```
Ageless woman, pinup style, full body shot, immortal dragon in human form revealed through
luminous reptilian eyes and iridescent scale hints.
<<Artist style:"Patrick Nagel"
mood:"1980s materialism, hedonic detachment, seductive power, aloof mystery. Cold glamour,
transactional posture, distant expressions, sharp cheekbone smirks."
medium:"Acrylic on stretched canvas, hand cut stencil serigraph, silkscreen ink bleed, opaque
color fields. Zero texture flat opacity, analog pigments, zero micro grain."
geometry:"Surgical precision, economy of means, frozen permanence, flattened perspective,
bisected negative space. Bold lines, stark porcelain/alabaster negative space dominant."
dna:"Pop art illustration, Japanese woodblock silhouette, Ukiyo e flat plane, bold minimalist
line work. Eastern print layouts merged with fashion illustration; high contrast ink boundaries,
zero 3D depth shading.">>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/returns>>

!! What the Renders Returned

''Seed A — the triptych sheet.'' Full figure at left on a flat cobalt rectangle, that rectangle
pasted onto a cream sheet whose margins run dense with ''illegible handwritten script''. Black
lacquered greatcoat, one shoulder built into a hard geometric wing; ''red'' at gloves, throat, and
boots and nowhere else. Face turned three-quarters away. Top-right panel takes the face close:
porcelain field, hard black brow-strokes, gold hoops, carmine lips — and ''yellow-green eyes''
carrying the entire reptilian tell. Bottom-right panel gives the dragon head in ''the same flat
plate grammar'' as the coat: blue-black and olive scales, a yellow slit eye, cream throat-scutes.

''Seed B — the cover.'' Blue trench with white topstitching, collar up. Blue-lensed rimless
spectacles pushed ''down the nose'', ice-blue eyes looking over them straight out of the frame.
Black lacquered glove, one long pale claw-nail raised vertical against red lips: ''the shush''.
Iridescent teardrop earrings reading as scale-hints. Red masthead bleeding off the top edge, a
column of small unreadable type down the left margin.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-it-caught>>

!! What the Register Caught

* ''The tell lives in the eyes alone.'' Everything else reads as a woman in very good outerwear.
  The scale-hints stay ornamental; the eyes do the work. This matches the canon of a Great Dragon
  arriving under a ''mana-muting glamour'' — the glamour holds everywhere except where she permits
  it not to.
* ''One grammar for both bodies.'' The dragon panel and the lacquered coat are painted in the same
  flat plates with the same ink boundaries. Scale and lacquer read as ''one material'', which is the
  right answer for a being who is not wearing a disguise so much as choosing a silhouette.
* ''The shush is her manner as a gesture.'' She answers short and spends real words only on the
  substrate. A claw-tipped finger to the lips renders that without a line of dialogue.
* ''The spectacles, pushed down.'' Smoked-glass gaze-courtesy belongs to the Gorgonne cabals and
  the harbor guilds who copied it. Wearing the courtesy and then ''declining'' it — lenses down,
  eyes out — reads as exactly the kind of manners she keeps.
* ''She stands on a page of writing nobody can read.'' Seed A mounts her figure on a field of
  illegible script. For a Patroness whose hoard was records, junk, and off-world artifacts, and who
  co-built an archive-network, the accident lands well enough to keep.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/craft-notes>>

!! Craft Notes (for the next seed)

* ''`zero micro grain` did not hold'' in Seed B — visible halftone and dotted stitch-lines
  throughout. The silkscreen clauses (`silkscreen ink bleed`, `hand cut stencil serigraph`) appear
  to outvote it. Choose one: press for true flat opacity ''or'' accept the print artifacts as part
  of the look.
* ''`full body shot` yielded a triptych'' in Seed A rather than a single figure. The multi-panel
  return reads well here; name it deliberately if it is wanted again.
* ''Red discipline'': Seed A confines red to throat, hands, and feet. Worth keeping as a stated
  palette rule rather than leaving to chance.
* ''Never fix the form.'' Any future seed should keep at least one element deliberately unstable
  between renders, so the boards stay honest about disagreeing.

<<~/ahu>>

